   "html": "<p>IHC transformed a central footprint at New York Comic Con into a fully immersive recreation of <strong>Camp Crystal Lake</strong>&nbsp;- a weathered cabin exterior giving way to richly detailed forest and shed interiors, brought to life by live theatrical performances and capped by a climactic scare moment inside Jason’s shed.</p><p>The result: a dual-purpose activation that doubled as a fully realized guest experience and a strategic content engine, giving press and creators a dedicated environment to capture the talent walkthrough and the experience’s signature scare moment alike. A virtual queue let fans reserve a spot, driving <strong>15k+&nbsp;sign-ups</strong> across the four-day run and sending hundreds of groups through the full experience.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "THE BUILD",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "html": "<p>A cabin facade jutted out from the walls to immerse guests into the world. A custom sign hung from a post at the line entrance, and a camp bulletin board had in-world easter eggs that guests could browse while they listened to excerpts from Radio Crystal Lake.&nbsp;The facade was covered in 360 key art, serving as a large scale photo moment.</p>"
    },
